# 13. Literature ownership / collision audit

## Kaijser

Subrectangular observation-word condition for filter convergence is classical.

## Kochman–Reeds

Unique ergodicity under the Kaijser condition and rank-one closure line are classical.

## Chigansky–van Handel

The qualitative finite/countable-state unique-ergodicity problem posed by Blackwell is solved; finite-state rank-one closure is essentially the right qualitative condition.

Therefore the lab must not frame filter unique ergodicity itself as an open historical problem.

## Shuval–Tal

This is a direct prior-art collision:

- subrectangular Birkhoff coefficients;
- arbitrary nonnegative matrices between contracting factors;
- products of contraction coefficients;
- number of nonoverlapping contracting occurrences;
- finite quantitative bounds on conditional mutual information.

Hence CWR-BP-090's "subrectangular words imply quantitative contraction" is classical and must be downgraded.

### Remaining candidate

The narrower synthesis that remains under audit is

\[
\boxed{
\text{contracting-word count}
\to
\text{conditional entire-future Le Cam null deficiency}
\to
\text{all-loss stopping certificate}.
}
\]

A search performed in this wave did not identify this exact formulation.

That is not evidence of novelty.

